	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
		You catch Bailey's sleeve. "Please wait. The fox is still inside."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
		You point back at the burning building. "The fox... You left <<person5>><<him>> inside."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
		You block the car door. "We're not leaving without the fox."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty">>
		"Wait, wait! What about the fox?"
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">>
		You grab Bailey's injured hand and pull <<him>> back towards the building. "You forgot someone. Go back."
	<<else>>
		"Why didn't you pull <<person5>><<him>> out with me?"
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<person2>>Robin gives you a confused look. "Who are you talking about? There wasn't anyone else trapped in there with you."
	<br><br>

	<<person1>>Bailey scoffs.
<</if>>
<br><br>

