:: Skyscraper Run Bailey Ask
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<person1>>

<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	"You... actually came," you say, "a-and you brought Robin."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"You came for me," you say. You reach for Robin's hand. "Thank you for bringing <<him>> too."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	You move close to Bailey before looking at Robin. "You both came. I knew you would."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"You made it," you say, pulling Robin towards you. "I was waiting for both of you."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty">>
	"You actually came for me instead of sitting on your ass," you say, "and you brought Robin over too."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">>
	You seize Bailey's sleeve. "You took long enough, but at least you had the sense to bring Robin."
<<else>>
	"You came for me," you say, "and you brought Robin with you."
<</if>>
<br><br>

Bailey's eyes meet yours briefly through the rearview mirror before <<he>> turns them back to the road. "Don't overthink it."

<<if !$wardrobe_residential_alleys>>
	<br><br>
	<<set $wardrobe_residential_alleys to 1>>
	"We moved your belongings to a storage unit near the orphanage," <<he>> says, handing you a key. "In the alleyways behind it. Number 22 is yours. Don't tell the others. They'll all want one."
<</if>>
<br><br>

Bailey starts the engine, and drives onto the boulevard.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Skyscraper Run Bailey 6]]>><</link>>
