:: Chef Opening Bailey Assure
<<endevent>>
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "cafe">><<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<npc Bailey>><<person1>>

<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	"I-I'm not going to say anything bad," you say. "T-The orphanage is my home..."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"You needn't worry," you say. "I intend to speak well of the place that raised me."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	You keep your voice low. "I'll say what you want. I won't cause trouble for the orphanage."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"I know what to say," you tell Bailey. "I can praise the orphanage without your help."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty">>
	"Relax. I'm not going to say anything about the orphanage," you shrug. "I live there, don't I?"
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">>
	"I could ruin your evening with one honest answer," you say. "Be grateful I'm choosing not to."
<<else>>
	"I won't say anything bad," you say. "Today isn't about you or the orphanage."
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<if C.npc.Bailey.dom lte 30>>
	Bailey's smile goes tight before <<he>> smooths <<his>> face out. "We'll see about that."
<<elseif C.npc.Bailey.dom gte 70>>
	Bailey's smile looks warm and real. "I know."
<<else>>
	Bailey's smile stays perfectly fake. <<He>> says nothing.
<</if>>
<br><br>

Bailey looks away from you. You realise that, for the first time since your arrival, you're no longer the centre of attention.
<br><br>

<<link [[Look|Chef Opening 7]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>


:: Chef Opening Praise
<<endevent>>
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "cafe">><<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<npc Bailey 1>><<person1>>

You look around the room. Bailey stares back. <<if C.npc.Bailey.dom lte 30>><<His>> gaze flickers between you and Quinn.<</if>> You put on your best smile and begin.
<br><br>

<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	You begin with the youth ward and the years you spent growing up beside Robin. Your voice shakes, but you continue by thanking the workers who kept you safe and the other orphans who worked beside you. You finish by crediting Bailey with teaching you how much effort it takes to build a life.
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	You welcome the guests, then guide them through a careful account of your childhood in the youth ward. You speak warmly about Robin, praise the staff, and draw attention to the work done by every orphan in Bailey's care. When you thank Bailey, you turn towards <<him>> so the whole room follows your lead.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	You repeat the parts of your childhood that Bailey would want the room to hear. The workers kept you safe, the other orphans worked hard, and Bailey prepared you for adult life. You leave out everything that might make <<him>> angry.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	You tell the room how you grew up with Robin and learned to support yourself beside the other orphans. You give the workers their share of the credit, then acknowledge that Bailey's demands prepared you to handle the pressure of this opening.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty">>
	You describe learning about work and discipline before you were old enough to understand either one. A few guests laugh when you admit that Bailey's lessons were rarely pleasant, but you finish by saying they prepared you for exactly this moment.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">>
	You praise the orphanage by listing what its children accomplish despite the pressure placed on them. You name Robin and the workers who helped you, then leave Bailey until the end. "<<He>> taught me what people can endure when failure isn't allowed," you say.
<<else>>
	You describe growing up in the youth ward beside Robin, then thank the workers and the other orphans. You explain what the orphanage gave you, what Bailey taught you, and how those lessons helped bring you here.
<</if>>
<br><br>

The audience listens in quiet admiration. Some wipe tears from their eyes. Others look unconvinced.
<br><br>

The employee you recognise from the orphanage has gone pale, refusing to meet your gaze. <<stress 12>><<trauma 6>><<ggstress>><<gtrauma>>
<br><br>

<<if $chef_gwylan>>
	You catch Gwylan's eye on the second floor. <<nnpc_He "Gwylan">> is smiling. Something flickers beneath the surface of <<nnpc_his "Gwylan">> face. It's there and gone, faster than you could identify it.
	<br><br>
<</if>>

Quinn smiles and nods along. <<nnpc_He "Quinn">> looks like someone watching things go exactly as planned.
<br><br>

<<if $chef_avery>>
	Avery is the only one not applauding, glass of whisky untouched. <<nnpc_Hes "Avery">> looking right at Bailey.
	<br><br>
<</if>>

<<person1>>You dare a glance at Bailey as you leave the podium. <<He>> is still looking at you<<if C.npc.Bailey.dom gte 70>>, wearing a disarming smile that almost looks real.<<else>>. <<His>> expression gives nothing away.<</if>><<npcincr Bailey love 2>><<npcincr Bailey dom 1>><<set $syndromeBaileyBuild += 1>><<set $baileyStockholmPoints.cafe to true>><<gglove "Bailey">><<gdom "Bailey">><<gbaileystock>>
<br><br>

The party begins in earnest. What do you want to do?
<br><br>

<<endevent>>
<<chefspeechoptions>>


:: Chef Opening Praise End
<<endevent>>
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "cafe">><<effects>>
<<npc Bailey>><<person1>>

The party winds down after a few hours. You head to the exit, but Bailey intercepts you.
<br><br>

<<He>> steps close. <<His>> hand finds the back of your neck.
<br><br>

<<if C.npc.Bailey.dom lte 30>>
	"So that head of yours isn't just for show. Good," <<he>> says with a sneer. The words are just for you. "Rent's still due, brat."
<<elseif C.npc.Bailey.dom gte 70>>
	"Useful, aren't you?" <<he>> says, <<his>> voice low enough only you can hear. "Rent's still due."
<<else>>
	"Don't get any ideas," <<he>> says quietly, so only you can hear. "Rent's still due."
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<He>> squeezes your neck once before releasing you and walking away.<<npcincr Bailey dom 1>><<gdom "Bailey">>
